#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/0
msgid ""
"Kaz, what kind of shape is that plant the\n"
"\"professor\" gave us in?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/1
msgid ""
"First time I laid eyes on it, I thought it was some\n"
"kind of joke.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/2
msgid ""
"It was a giant birdhouse - seagulls everywhere.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/3
msgid ""
"We eventually scraped off most of the rust and\n"
"bird crap.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/4
msgid ""
"The underlying structure's intact - a little elbow\n"
"grease and we should be in business.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/5
msgid ""
"Who used to own it, anyway?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/6
msgid ""
"Whatever shape it's in now, somebody sank some\n"
"serious money into building it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/7
msgid ""
"From what I can tell, an American university built it\n"
"as a research platform\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/8
msgid ""
"for ocean thermal energy conversion, \"OTEC.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/9
msgid ""
"The name's still on some of the rusty old power\n"
"turbines.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/10
msgid ""
"I'm guessing they must have had government and\n"
"corporate assistance to build it, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/11
msgid ""
"But they couldn't solve the thermal efficiency\n"
"problem, and the project was canceled.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/12
msgid ""
"Then after the university abandoned it,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/13
msgid ""
"a KGB front company scooped it up for next to\n"
"nothing... At least, that's my theory.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/14
msgid ""
"How'd the KGB manage to buy a plant built with\n"
"American capital, front company or not?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/15
msgid ""
"Yeah, that \"professor\" is quite the operator.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/16
msgid ""
"One other thing:\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/17
msgid ""
"the plant's set up so that it can join up with other\n"
"plants of the same standard.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/18
msgid ""
"So they were originally planning on expanding the\n"
"place, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/19
msgid ""
"Hey, let's give it a shot?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/20
msgid ""
"We can get some more people together and build\n"
"this place up into a proper home for MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x944b0/21
msgid ""
"You're with me on this, right, Boss?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x94d00/0
msgid ""
"The new plant is a hex type. That gives it more\n"
"surface area than previous types\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x94d00/1
msgid ""
"and also makes it easier to plan expansions. We're\n"
"gonna make this place huge.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x94d00/2
msgid ""
"Hex, huh. Like a beehive.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x94d00/3
msgid ""
"Nothing wrong with that. They say the honeycomb\n"
"design is one of the strongest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x94d00/4
msgid ""
"I hear they're even thinking of using it in tank\n"
"armor.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x94d00/5
msgid ""
"Good enough for me. I'll see about finding us some\n"
"worker bees.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/148/0x94d00/6
msgid ""
"Appreciate it, Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you can use the Fulton Surface-to-air\n"
"Recovery System\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/1
msgid ""
"to send prisoners and unconscious mercenaries\n"
"you encounter back to the Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/2
msgid ""
"I know you've used the Fulton before,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/3
msgid ""
"but just to make sure I'm not missing anything,\n"
"let's review the steps.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 18822..18947
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_myo_rad_0080_000_0
#. timeline 6534..6757
#: codec/1/149/0x95220/4
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/18
#: codec/1/218/0xda210/26
#: codec/1/233/0xe9630/15
#: codec/2/915/0x393270/19
#: codec/2/916/0x394bd0/8
msgid ""
"OK.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/5
msgid ""
"First, attach a balloon to the unconscious enemy\n"
"or captured prisoner.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/6
msgid ""
"Right. I hook a wire to the their waist, and on the\n"
"other end of the wire there's a helium balloon.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/7
msgid ""
"Right. Then we'll send over a chopper to catch the\n"
"floating balloon with its recovery hook and reel it\n"
"up into its cargo hold.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/8
msgid ""
"And that's it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/9
msgid ""
"And that's it. We finished installing the recovery\n"
"hook on the Huey...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/10
msgid ""
"Wait, Kaz, something doesn't make sense about this\n"
"whole process.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/11
msgid ""
"Not this again...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/12
msgid ""
"Normally, Fulton recovery is for when you're using\n"
"fixed-wing aircraft.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/13
msgid ""
"With a helicopter, isn't it simpler to land and pick\n"
"up directly?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/14
msgid ""
"Listen, Snake, you're gonna be calling for\n"
"recoveries repeatedly throughout your mission.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/15
msgid ""
"We want to keep the risk of taking enemy fire to a\n"
"minimum.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/16
msgid ""
"The best way to get that done that is to do the\n"
"recovery in a high-speed fly-by.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/17
msgid ""
"That's what the Fulton Surface-to-air Recovery\n"
"System is for.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/18
msgid ""
"Uh huh... what's the real reason?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/19
msgid ""
"Helicopters are cheaper.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/20
msgid ""
"And the repair bills will start adding up once the\n"
"bullets start flying...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/21
msgid ""
"Thought so. Kaz, I know we need to keep costs\n"
"down, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/22
msgid ""
"Boss, you really need to get rid of this whole Army\n"
"mentality. We're not the Pentagon.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/23
msgid ""
"We don't have billions of taxpayer dollars to play\n"
"with. And besides...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/24
msgid ""
"Fine, fine. Just pick a reason that makes sense.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/25
msgid ""
"Helicopters have quicker response time. Sounds\n"
"strange, yeah, but it works great, I promise.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/26
msgid ""
"You'll get used to it before long.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95220/27
msgid ""
"Yeah, I hope so.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 501..2089
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/0
msgid ""
"Remember why we created MSF, Snake: to provide\n"
"military force to whoever needs it,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 2103..3162
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/1
msgid ""
"wherever they are, regardless of nation or ideology.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 3190..3775
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/2
msgid ""
"Our beliefs aren't all that lofty...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 3775..4639
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/3
msgid ""
"We just won't be the tools of any one country.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 4639..5503
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/4
msgid ""
"Exactly. We know only how to fight...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 5517..6561
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/5
msgid ""
"but we refuse to live our lives at the whim of the\n"
"state.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 6575..7467
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/6
msgid ""
"The MSF seal is patterned after Pangaea,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 7481..8540
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/7
msgid ""
"the supercontinent from 250 million years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 8623..9348
#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/8
msgid ""
"Back then, the whole world was one landmass.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/9
msgid ""
"One world. No gaps, no rifts.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/149/0x95c80/10
msgid ""
"Our strength will take us back there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 529..1657
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/0
msgid ""
"What about you, Kaz? Any interest in expanding\n"
"MSF?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 1685..2089
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/1
msgid ""
"You'd better believe it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 2117..3385
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/2
msgid ""
"I want to make us into an organization that doesn't\n"
"take orders from any country\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 3427..3859
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/3
msgid ""
"- just like you were saying.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 3900..4904
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/4
msgid ""
"We have to be strong, strong enough to defend\n"
"ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 4931..5962
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/5
msgid ""
"We need money, too - money to train soldiers to\n"
"fight.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 6018..7565
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/6
msgid ""
"The way I see it, we make MSF into something\n"
"along the lines of a new kind of business.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 7606..9083
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/7
msgid ""
"A contractor providing the full range of military\n"
"services. Not just combat,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 9111..10379
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/8
msgid ""
"but logistics, training, weapons, outfitting and R&D...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 10407..11758
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/9
msgid ""
"Combining the small footprint and exceptional\n"
"performance of Special Forces\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 11758..12831
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/10
msgid ""
"with the raw military might of a full regular army.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 12914..14043
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/11
msgid ""
"Only with that kind of power can we break free of\n"
"nation-states.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 14057..14503
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/12
msgid ""
"What I need from you, Boss,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 14531..15840
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/13
msgid ""
"is to go out and find guys we can bring back here\n"
"using Fulton recovery.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 15896..16648
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/14
msgid ""
"Then tell us what assignment to use them for.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_000_0
#. timeline 16662..17150
#: codec/1/150/0x96040/15
msgid ""
"I'll take care of the rest.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 487..1044
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/0
msgid ""
"Your old mentor, The Boss...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 1058..2020
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/1
msgid ""
"She was known in the West as the \"Mother of\n"
"Special Forces,\" right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 2326..2758
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/2
msgid ""
"Nothing but propaganda.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 2772..3691
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/3
msgid ""
"Actually, it's not all that far from the truth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 3719..5433
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/4
msgid ""
"I heard the KGB just set up a counter-sabotage\n"
"cell. Alpha Group, I think they call it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 5461..6575
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/5
msgid ""
"There's even a rumor that West Germany created\n"
"a counter-terrorist unit within its\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 6575..7565
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/6
msgid ""
"border police after the debacle at the Munich\n"
"Olympics.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 7578..8442
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/7
msgid ""
"Back home in the States, they've got the illustrious\n"
"Green Berets,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 8442..9418
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/8
msgid ""
"the SEALs, and your personal creation,\n"
"FOXHOUND...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 9431..10281
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/9
msgid ""
"The seeds sown by The Boss are beginning to\n"
"sprout.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 10337..11772
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/10
msgid ""
"Same goes for MSF, right? In creating it, you were\n"
"carrying on the will of The Boss.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 12260..13625
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/11
msgid ""
"She taught me how to fight, the hard way - she\n"
"beat it into me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 13639..15144
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/12
msgid ""
"And now thanks to her, we can take on missions\n"
"other than just conventional combat.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0070_010_0
#. timeline 15227..16620
#: codec/1/150/0x96600/13
msgid ""
"After all, we've got the same mother as the Army's\n"
"Special Forces.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 515..1894
#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/0
msgid ""
"You know, Snake, you're right. As long as we're\n"
"\"soldiers without borders,\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 1922..2856
#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/1
msgid ""
"we're going to be a target. We need our own\n"
"deterrent.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 3037..4137
#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/2
msgid ""
"We're going to be stepping into a lot of different\n"
"conflicts as we roam the world.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 4137..5642
#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/3
msgid ""
"Each one unique, and with its own set of\n"
"geography, ideologies, and politics.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 5670..6659
#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/4
msgid ""
"If we're going to intervene in those kinds of\n"
"situations,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/5
msgid ""
"we need the threat of a Metal Gear.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/6
msgid ""
"...Unless we want to end up like Che Guevara did in\n"
"Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/7
msgid ""
"Well said. Our army without borders doesn't have a\n"
"land to call home.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/8
msgid ""
"We're nomads. Wanderers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/9
msgid ""
"What we need now is a sheepdog to guard our\n"
"flock.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 2187..2382
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 2131..2368
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0040_000_0
#. timeline 6520..6645
#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/10
#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/1
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/2
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/2
#: codec/1/200/0xc8b50/1
#: codec/1/203/0xcb100/7
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/10
msgid ""
"Right.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/11
msgid ""
"Maybe it's not the way The Boss would have gone\n"
"about it...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/12
msgid ""
"But there are places in this world that need us -\n"
"and soldiers that need MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/13
msgid ""
"And as long as we're needed, we'll keep on moving.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/14
msgid ""
"Ours is a journey that never ends.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/150/0x96b70/15
msgid ""
"We're the real Peace Walkers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/0
msgid ""
"Still can't believe Professor Gálvez was KGB...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/1
msgid ""
"Well, like the \"professor\" said,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/2
msgid ""
"Moscow's hell bent on communizing Latin America.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, the Cuban intel services are all in the KGB's\n"
"pocket.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/4
msgid ""
"You don't think he's got some kind of ulterior\n"
"motive?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/5
msgid ""
"If the CIA is up to something, it's only natural that\n"
"the KGB wants to know about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/6
msgid ""
"But I doubt they're showing us their full hand.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97110/7
msgid ""
"We'd better watch our backs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97400/0
msgid ""
"What do you think, Kaz? Why did Paz come all the\n"
"way to Colombia herself?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97400/1
msgid ""
"It is a long trip to make just to be Exhibit A in\n"
"Gálvez's sales pitch...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x97400/2
msgid ""
"She's only 16 - still a kid. Maybe we should take\n"
"her wish for peace at face value.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x975b0/0
msgid ""
"Remember that habit Paz had, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x975b0/1
msgid ""
"How she always had her index finger on her upper\n"
"lip like this?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x975b0/2
msgid ""
"Yeah. It bugged me ever since we first met her...\n"
"Never figured her for a snuff user.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x975b0/3
msgid ""
"I can't believe we never noticed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x975b0/4
msgid ""
"She used the kind where you keep a pouch of leaf\n"
"in your upper jaw\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x975b0/5
msgid ""
"and let it absorb through your gums.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/151/0x975b0/6
msgid ""
"She might not have been used to it. Probably used\n"
"her finger to keep it in place.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 487..1490
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/0
msgid ""
"How could Paz... We were going to start a band\n"
"together...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 1490..2326
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/1
msgid ""
"She was posing as a KGB agent, too?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 2326..3204
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/2
msgid ""
"She must have put on the act to get close to\n"
"Gálvez.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 3260..3747
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/3
msgid ""
"Wonder how much Coldman knew...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 3761..4848
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/4
msgid ""
"But the whole time she was working for some\n"
"organization called \"Cipher.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 5001..5837
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/5
msgid ""
"\"Cipher\"... Ring any bells, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 5851..7272
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/6
msgid ""
"Cipher... Cipher... it means \"code.\" Or \"zero\" in\n"
"Arabic numerals.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 7272..7551
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/7
msgid ""
"Zero...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 7551..7913
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/8
msgid ""
"Does that mean something to you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 7913..8261
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/9
msgid ""
"Not sure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 8275..9445
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/10
msgid ""
"Hmm. You know, \"cipher\" and \"zero\" were basically\n"
"the same word.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 9473..10017
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/11
msgid ""
"It's a linguistic redundancy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 10017..10797
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/12
msgid ""
"The word stems from the Sanskrit \"shunya\"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 10811..11702
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/13
msgid ""
"It corresponds to the Buddhist concept of\n"
"emptiness.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 11702..12524
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/14
msgid ""
"In Buddhism, \"shunya\" means hollow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 12580..13778
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/15
msgid ""
"It supposedly refers to something that's swollen\n"
"and empty on the inside.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0100_020_1
#. timeline 13778..15060
#: codec/1/151/0x97880/16
msgid ""
"A big, swollen emptiness... just like outer space.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 501..1239
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/0
msgid ""
"They say nuclear weapons are the reason we\n"
"haven't seen\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 1239..2145
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/1
msgid ""
"conflict on a global scale since World War II.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 2173..3009
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/2
msgid ""
"The thought that your opponent might launch\n"
"nukes against you\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 3009..3831
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/3
msgid ""
"sort of makes it tough to start an armed conflict.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 3859..4931
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/4
msgid ""
"Especially now that they've got inter-continental\n"
"ballistic missiles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 4973..5349
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/5
msgid ""
"Nowhere is safe.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 5363..6534
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/6
msgid ""
"Of course, all that has caused military expenditures\n"
"to skyrocket...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 6548..8066
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/7
msgid ""
"Well, the only way to ward off a preemptive strike\n"
"is to flaunt your own nuclear stockpile.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 8080..8958
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/8
msgid ""
"And that's caused their numbers to increase\n"
"exponentially.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 8972..10546
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/9
msgid ""
"Not just with regards to destructive power, but in\n"
"terms of targeting technology, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 10630..11814
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/10
msgid ""
"Now they can hit a target halfway across the\n"
"world with pinpoint accuracy.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 11842..13277
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/11
msgid ""
"In a way, the space race was a demonstration of\n"
"that technological progress.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 13277..14614
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/12
msgid ""
"And as a result of all that, we now have mutually\n"
"assured destruction...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 14614..15199
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/13
msgid ""
"It's the ultimate form of deterrence.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 15199..16342
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/14
msgid ""
"No one's going to launch their nukes knowing\n"
"they'll be obliterated in return.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0120_000_1
#. timeline 16342..18139
#: codec/1/152/0x984e0/15
msgid ""
"...I dunno. The chance of somebody hitting the\n"
"button by mistake is never zero.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 501..1532
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/0
msgid ""
"You're right - even with peace guaranteed by MAD,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 1532..2145
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/1
msgid ""
"there's always the risk of an accident.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 2145..3399
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/2
msgid ""
"Nobody wants the world to end on account of\n"
"some machine's malfunctioning.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 3399..4945
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/3
msgid ""
"On the other hand, thanks to deterrence, we\n"
"haven't had a world war since 1945.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 4973..5795
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/4
msgid ""
"You've gotta admit, it has been pretty peaceful.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 5921..6394
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/5
msgid ""
"Not that it matters to us.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 6394..7718
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/6
msgid ""
"People point at the nuclear arms and space races\n"
"and call it a Cold War.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 7787..8930
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/7
msgid ""
"I say if they're not shooting at each other, why not\n"
"call it world peace?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 8930..10421
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/8
msgid ""
"Doesn't mean war is gone. Look at Korea. Look at\n"
"Vietnam.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 10421..11284
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/9
msgid ""
"Well, yeah, but I'm talking in relative terms here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 11284..12190
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/10
msgid ""
"Besides, if war died out completely we'd be SOL.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 12190..12733
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/11
msgid ""
"...We're not warmongers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0130_000_0
#. timeline 12733..13764
#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/12
msgid ""
"And yet we can't survive in a world that's at peace.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/152/0x98b30/13
msgid ""
"You've got a point...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 473..1462
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/0
msgid ""
"So it's been more than ten years since the Cuban\n"
"Missile Crisis, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 1476..1992
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/1
msgid ""
"I don't think we'll ever forget it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 2201..3636
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/2
msgid ""
"No kidding. Those 13 days starting October 15,\n"
"1962\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 3719..4834
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/3
msgid ""
"were probably the closest we ever came to all-out\n"
"nuclear war.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 4876..6422
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/4
msgid ""
"The Russians deployed nuclear missiles to Cuba.\n"
"America responded with a naval blockade.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 6478..7300
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/5
msgid ""
"Then Russia shot down an American spy plane...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 7383..7927
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/6
msgid ""
"I was still a teenager back then.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 8010..9139
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/7
msgid ""
"But I remember what it felt like to be one step\n"
"away from nuclear war\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 9209..9682
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/8
msgid ""
"- the adults were freaking out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 9710..10295
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/9
msgid ""
"If it wasn't for the Cuban Missile Crisis,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 10295..11284
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/10
msgid ""
"there might never have been an Operation Snake\n"
"Eater. And...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 11284..12413
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/11
msgid ""
"What's the matter, Snake? It's not like you to get\n"
"all hypothetical.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 12441..14266
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/12
msgid ""
"Hm... I guess not. It was the reassessment after\n"
"the Missile Crisis\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 14266..15770
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/13
msgid ""
"that paved the way for the hotline between\n"
"Moscow and Washington, and also for Détente.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_000_0
#. timeline 15854..16356
#: codec/1/153/0x99020/14
msgid ""
"That's irony for you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 473..2006
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/0
msgid ""
"The Treaty of Tlatelolco was enacted to make\n"
"Latin America into a nuclear-free zone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 2131..3608
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/1
msgid ""
"It bans the testing, use, manufacture, production,\n"
"acquisition, storage,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 3622..4221
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/2
msgid ""
"and deployment of nuclear weapons.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 4360..4876
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/3
msgid ""
"The impetus was pretty obvious:\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 4917..6018
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/4
msgid ""
"the series of crises triggered by the deployment of\n"
"nukes in Cuba.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 6046..7648
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/5
msgid ""
"Not hard to imagine. Those 13 days had the whole\n"
"world frozen in fear.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 7676..9167
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/6
msgid ""
"Of course, the country that started it all - Cuba -\n"
"hasn't actually ratified it yet.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 9209..10072
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/7
msgid ""
"Still, the treaty's backed by over 20 countries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 10128..11103
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/8
msgid ""
"Anyone flouting it risks becoming an international\n"
"pariah.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 11145..12023
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/9
msgid ""
"True. OPANAL would investigate, no doubt.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 12051..13597
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/10
msgid ""
"I heard they used Japan's Three Non-Nuclear\n"
"Principles as their model when they drew up the\n"
"treaty.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 13695..14935
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/11
msgid ""
"I think the Treaty of Tlatelolco might have been\n"
"their way of asking nuclear powers\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 14962..15436
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/12
msgid ""
"not to use nukes against them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 15562..16606
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/13
msgid ""
"That's the biggest difference between the treaty\n"
"and the Three Principles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0140_010_0
#. timeline 16676..17275
#: codec/1/153/0x995a0/14
msgid ""
"I guess you could call it a fourth principle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 487..1128
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/0
msgid ""
"Hey Snake, mind if I ask you something?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 1407..2117
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/1
msgid ""
"Since when did you start asking permission?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 2145..3803
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/2
msgid ""
"..Ha. So, you used to be part of a CIA paramilitary\n"
"unit, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 3803..3984
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/3
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/24
msgid ""
"That's right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 3998..4569
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/4
msgid ""
"Ever do any ops in Central America?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 4583..5935
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/5
msgid ""
"No, not personally. But there were other units who\n"
"did all kinds of stuff.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 5962..6910
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/6
msgid ""
"I remember the Bay of Pigs invasion back in '61.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 6993..7467
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/7
msgid ""
"The papers had a field day with it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 7481..9236
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/8
msgid ""
"\"Operation Zapata\" - that was the CIA codename.\n"
"The whole thing went south.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 9250..10142
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/9
msgid ""
"Then there was Che Guevara being hunted down in\n"
"Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 10226..10950
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/10
msgid ""
"I heard the CIA had a hand in that, too...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 10950..12357
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/11
msgid ""
"There were several units similar to mine. MSP,\n"
"SOG...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 12427..13792
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/12
msgid ""
"They'd recruit former Special Forces, train them as\n"
"intelligence agents, and send them on\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 13792..14767
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/13
msgid ""
"\"deniable\" covert paramilitary operations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 14837..15896
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/14
msgid ""
"One of those units trained the Bolivian Army in\n"
"counter-guerilla tactics....\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 15924..16537
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/15
msgid ""
"...And then had them shoot El Che.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0160_000_0
#. timeline 16551..17052
#: codec/1/154/0x9a230/16
msgid ""
"So the story goes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 501..1657
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/0
msgid ""
"Around here, they say \"La CIA\", instead of \"C-I-A,\"\n"
"huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2117..3218
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/1
msgid ""
"Nothing strange about it. That's how it's\n"
"pronounced when you read it in Spanish.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 3232..4472
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/2
msgid ""
"It has the feminine noun ending \"a,\" so they use\n"
"the article \"la.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4486..5572
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/3
msgid ""
"Apparently some people have even taken to using\n"
"the term UCLA.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5586..6241
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/4
msgid ""
"That's a new one to me. What's it mean?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 6241..7328
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/5
msgid ""
"It stands for \"Unilaterally Controlled Latino Assets.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7342..7774
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/6
msgid ""
"...Meaning their local agents?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7787..8791
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/7
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's the idea. Washington uses them like\n"
"pawns,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 8791..9571
#: codec/1/154/0x9a7f0/8
msgid ""
"and nobody knows who they really are or what\n"
"they're doing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/0
msgid ""
"Can you believe the CIA and the KGB were actually\n"
"in cahoots?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/1
msgid ""
"Never thought I'd see that at the station chief\n"
"level...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/2
msgid ""
"But I've heard stories of operatives in the field\n"
"being on friendly terms.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/3
msgid ""
"Seriously?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/4
msgid ""
"Most espionage takes place in political hotspots, as\n"
"you'd expect.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/5
msgid ""
"But there aren't that many of those kinds of\n"
"places. Especially in a small country.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/6
msgid ""
"Hang around long enough, and you're bound to run\n"
"into fellow spies, like it or not.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/7
msgid ""
"You start saying hello, and soon enough you're\n"
"eating dinner together...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/8
msgid ""
"Strange bedfellows, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/9
msgid ""
"I dunno about that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/10
msgid ""
"At any rate, this kind of fiasco is what happens\n"
"when spies get too familiar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/11
msgid ""
"Hard to believe,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/12
msgid ""
"but some people will betray anyone and anything if\n"
"it suits their interests.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/13
msgid ""
"The strength of HUMINT is in its appeal to human\n"
"emotions,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/14
msgid ""
"but its weakness is in its susceptibility to those\n"
"same emotions.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/15
msgid ""
"That's why the tide in the intelligence world is\n"
"shifting toward SIGINT.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/154/0x9ab70/16
msgid ""
"A network of cold, digital data, where feelings are\n"
"irrelevant.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you got a sec?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/1
#: codec/2/915/0x393270/1
msgid ""
"What's up?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/2
msgid ""
"Prime Minister Gairy of Grenada is asking the UN\n"
"to set up an agency\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/3
msgid ""
"to study the \"UFO problem.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/4
msgid ""
"Grenada... That island in the Caribbean?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/5
msgid ""
"He gave the press a bunch of photos - says they\n"
"prove the existence of UFOs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/6
msgid ""
"One of them caught my eye.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/7
msgid ""
"That's the...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/8
msgid ""
"Yep... The weapon Huey called the Chrysalis.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/9
msgid ""
"...Kaz, this is the photo I gave to Chico.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/10
msgid ""
"He said something about selling it off as a photo\n"
"of a UFO...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/11
msgid ""
"Looks like it found its way into the pages of a\n"
"magazine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/12
msgid ""
"But... why would the prime minister of a country\n"
"believe tabloid trash like that?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/13
msgid ""
"There's been reports all over the Americas of\n"
"abductions and cattle mutilations, lately.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/14
msgid ""
"You think they're true?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/15
msgid ""
"I think the CIA might be involved.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/16
msgid ""
"If they are, then Gairy could be...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/17
msgid ""
"I know. If he digs too deep, he's gonna get himself\n"
"into trouble.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/18
msgid ""
"But Grenada's right next door to Cuba.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/19
msgid ""
"I guess that would make it tough for the CIA to\n"
"intervene, in a sense.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/20
msgid ""
"Upsetting the domestic balance of power could\n"
"cause it to go Red all of a sudden.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/21
msgid ""
"True... Well, in any case it's not like we can do\n"
"anything about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/22
msgid ""
"Just wanted to let you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b1c0/23
msgid ""
"Gotcha. I'll be careful not to let any more photos\n"
"leak.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/0
msgid ""
"So I hear Amanda mistook you for Che Guevara,\n"
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/1
msgid ""
"That's not too bad, huh?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/2
msgid ""
"Yeah, right. I'm not even worthy of polishing his\n"
"boots.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/3
msgid ""
"Don't be so modest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/4
msgid ""
"From where I'm standing, your men see you as a\n"
"great man.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/5
msgid ""
"As great as \"the century's most complete human\n"
"being\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/6
msgid ""
"That's Sartre, right? Well, there's hardly been a\n"
"more iconic figure of his times than Che.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/7
msgid ""
"He was more than that. He was a true\n"
"revolutionary, and a great warrior.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/8
msgid ""
"I'm with you there. Can you believe that when he\n"
"first went to Cuba with Fidel,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/9
msgid ""
"they only had 12 guys with them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/10
msgid ""
"But they rallied. They brought in new recruits,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/11
msgid ""
"won the support of the peasants, expanded their\n"
"organization...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/12
msgid ""
"And in the end, they overthrew the Batista regime...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/13
msgid ""
"People flocked to them because they were honest.\n"
"They won because they were strong.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/14
msgid ""
"Those are the qualities that make men great.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/15
msgid ""
"You know, we're kind of in the same boat they\n"
"were back then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/16
msgid ""
"Here we are, a handful of mercenaries\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/17
msgid ""
"taking on an army backed by the United States.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/18
msgid ""
"Yeah, we've got a long way to go.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/19
msgid ""
"But we've got to keep on going. It's not just about\n"
"winning in battle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/20
msgid ""
"You need to think about recruiting people and\n"
"growing this operation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0580_000_0
#. timeline 13527..13848
#: codec/1/155/0x9b990/21
#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/7
#: codec/1/178/0xb2060/14
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/40
#: codec/2/905/0x389770/22
msgid ""
"Got it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 501..1142
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/0
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake, I've been thinking...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 1170..2284
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/1
msgid ""
"Maybe Che couldn't find a place for himself outside\n"
"the battlefield, either.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 2298..2535
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0080_000_0
#. timeline 2465..2730
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/2
#: codec/1/198/0xc62d0/1
#: codec/1/224/0xe0990/9
#: codec/1/246/0xf6a00/2
msgid ""
"How so?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 2549..3803
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/3
msgid ""
"He led the Cuban Revolution to victory. That's\n"
"quite an accomplishment.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 3831..4625
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/4
msgid ""
"He could have called it quits there and nobody\n"
"would have blamed him.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 4653..6102
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/5
msgid ""
"But he left behind a loving family and a cabinet\n"
"post to plunge back into the struggle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 6116..7091
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/6
msgid ""
"First in the Congo, then in Bolivia - where he met\n"
"his end.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 7105..8526
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/7
msgid ""
"You're overthinking things. Che went back to the\n"
"battlefield because he was needed there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 8582..9376
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/8
msgid ""
"Read his \"Farewell Letter,\" then you'll understand.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 9390..10351
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/9
msgid ""
"Some say he was too idealistic to fit in with a\n"
"government.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 10365..11103
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/10
msgid ""
"Too many scruples, most likely.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 11117..11382
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/11
msgid ""
"Maybe so...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 11396..12343
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/12
msgid ""
"But I still can't help thinking the reason you look\n"
"up to Che\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 12385..13165
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/13
msgid ""
"is because you see something of yourself in him...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 13235..14071
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/14
msgid ""
"You left your country behind and plunged into\n"
"battle.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 14154..15269
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/15
msgid ""
"You wander from one battlefield to another, going\n"
"wherever you're needed...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 15283..16871
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/16
msgid ""
"Che was a revolutionary as well as a warrior. He\n"
"took up arms to fight for his beliefs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 16885..18919
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/17
msgid ""
"I don't do what I do for any ideology. I'm a warrior.\n"
"Nothing more, nothing less.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0200_010_0
#. timeline 18961..20591
#: codec/1/156/0x9c120/18
msgid ""
"OK, Boss. You're right. Just wanted to see how we\n"
"stacked up against a real hero.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/0
msgid ""
"Boss, did you ever read Che Guevara's book\n"
"\"Guerrilla Warfare\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/1
msgid ""
"I, uh... can't remember if I got to that one or not.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/2
msgid ""
"You should have, that's why I lent it to you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/3
msgid ""
"A lot of the guerrilla tactics it covers apply to\n"
"sneaking missions, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/4
msgid ""
"Che was one of the first people to articulate the\n"
"theory of guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/5
msgid ""
"T.E. Lawrence - \"Lawrence of Arabia\" - was another\n"
"one.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/6
msgid ""
"And Mao Zedong and his \"On Protracted War\"...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/7
msgid ""
"Theory aside, Nicaragua's General Sandino\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/8
msgid ""
"was one of the first to put guerrilla tactics into\n"
"practice.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/9
msgid ""
"Which explains why the Sandinistas named\n"
"themselves after him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/10
msgid ""
"If you think about it, guerrilla warfare itself has\n"
"been around since ancient times.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/11
msgid ""
"There's only so many ways a small group can\n"
"upset a large army.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/12
msgid ""
"There was a samurai in Japan who excelled in\n"
"guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/13
msgid ""
"No kidding?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/14
msgid ""
"Kusunoki Masashige. He was a warrior who lived in\n"
"the medieval era.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/15
msgid ""
"He used unconventional tactics to help overthrow\n"
"the Kamakura Shogunate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0050_010_0
#. timeline 2661..2953
#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/16
#: codec/1/244/0xf4740/2
msgid ""
"Like what?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/17
msgid ""
"Trojan Horse-style maneuvers and decoys to\n"
"confuse the enemy...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/18
msgid ""
"The best one was when the enemy was climbing\n"
"his castle walls\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/19
msgid ""
"- he dumped boiling water and human excrement\n"
"on them...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/20
msgid ""
"Sounds great. Let's put it in the MSF playbook.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/21
msgid ""
"...You're not serious, are you, Boss?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/22
msgid ""
"Why not? We've got plenty of crap to unload.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/156/0x9c850/23
msgid ""
"Uh.... yeah. I'll think about it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 445..1030
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/0
msgid ""
"What's wrong, Kaz? You sound beat.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 1044..2020
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/1
msgid ""
"Yeah, the problems never seem to end around\n"
"here...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 2034..3190
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/2
msgid ""
"You should take a break. Share a cup of mate with\n"
"the other guys.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 3287..3831
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/3
msgid ""
"It'll give you a chance to connect with them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 3859..4931
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/4
msgid ""
"I wonder if Che and his men ever sat around drank\n"
"mate.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 4945..6088
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/5
msgid ""
"I bet they did. Che was famous for his love of the\n"
"stuff.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 7523..8930
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/6
msgid ""
"Man, whoever thought of this was a genius. You\n"
"can put it in a gourd and carry it around,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 8944..10142
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/7
msgid ""
"and there's a special straw with a filter attached\n"
"so you can drink it anytime.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 10156..11382
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/8
msgid ""
"That's not all. It's full of essential vitamins and\n"
"minerals, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 11521..12301
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/9
msgid ""
"Nice to have in a guerrilla war when food is short.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 12315..13904
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/10
msgid ""
"Yeah, I wish I had a chance to share some with a\n"
"blonde Parisienne when I was out hiking.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 14043..14461
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/11
msgid ""
"...How do you know about that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0230_000_0
#. timeline 14461..16370
#: codec/1/157/0x9d0b0/12
msgid ""
"It takes a thief - or should I say it takes a snake -\n"
"to know one, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 487..1128
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/0
msgid ""
"The year the Cuban Revolution was won,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 1212..2256
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/1
msgid ""
"Che visited Japan as a member of an economic\n"
"delegation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 2368..3037
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/2
msgid ""
"While he was there, he visited Hiroshima.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 3037..3301
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/3
msgid ""
"Hiroshima...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 3329..4137
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/4
msgid ""
"Since he was there to discuss economic issues,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 4207..5057
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/5
msgid ""
"Hiroshima wasn't part of the original itinerary.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 5126..6631
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/6
msgid ""
"Some said the Ministry of Foreign Affairs didn't\n"
"want to let him go. But he went anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 6687..7578
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/7
msgid ""
"He snuck out of his hotel and took an overnight\n"
"train.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7829..8930
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/8
msgid ""
"Traveling guerrilla-style - sounds like Che, all right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 8958..10309
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/9
msgid ""
"He visited the Peace Memorial Museum and the\n"
"Atomic Bomb Survivors Hospital.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 10421..10992
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/10
msgid ""
"Apparently it gave him quite a shock.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 11020..12204
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/11
msgid ""
"As a doctor, it must have been painful for him to\n"
"see how the victims suffered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 12232..12733
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/12
msgid ""
"Nukes destroy everything...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 12747..13123
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/13
msgid ""
"He was quoted as saying,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 13263..14475
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/14
msgid ""
"\"They put you through this, and still you do\n"
"whatever America says?\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 14531..15743
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/15
msgid ""
"...Those words really hit me hard. Especially when I\n"
"think of my mom.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 15770..17261
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/16
msgid ""
"He said something else, too: \"Let us all love\n"
"Hiroshima, and its people.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 17303..18752
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/17
msgid ""
"I can believe it. Che never managed to numb\n"
"himself to other people's pain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0240_000_0
#. timeline 18975..20089
#: codec/1/157/0x9d5c0/18
msgid ""
"That's why people loved him. And why he died.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/0
msgid ""
"That bandanna you're always wearing - that thing's\n"
"a real antique.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/1
msgid ""
"Ever think about getting a new one?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/2
msgid ""
"This one's fine.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/3
msgid ""
"Come on, we can't have our Boss wearing a\n"
"raggedy old thing like that...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/4
msgid ""
"It was a gift, OK? It wouldn't be right to get rid of\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/5
msgid ""
"It was? OK, then... Speaking of which,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/6
msgid ""
"Che supposedly had a black scarf he used to take\n"
"everywhere with him.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/7
msgid ""
"A scarf?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/8
msgid ""
"One of his comrades gave it to him when he broke\n"
"his arm in battle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/9
msgid ""
"Che used that silk scarf as a sling...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/10
msgid ""
"and the comrade who gave it to him became his\n"
"second wife.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/11
msgid ""
"Aleida, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/12
msgid ""
"Even after his arm healed up, he never went\n"
"anywhere without that scarf.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/13
msgid ""
"What about you? You get that bandanna from\n"
"someone special?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/157/0x9dc70/14
msgid ""
"No, nothing like that. It's... important to me, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/0
msgid ""
"You were saying Japan has a peace constitution,\n"
"too?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/1
msgid ""
"Yep. Japan renounced war in Article 9 of its\n"
"constitution.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/2
msgid ""
"Aspiring sincerely to an international peace based\n"
"on justice and order...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/3
msgid ""
"...the Japanese people forever renounce war as a\n"
"sovereign right of the nation\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/4
msgid ""
"and the threat or use of force as means of\n"
"settling international disputes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/5
msgid ""
"In order to accomplish the aim of the preceding\n"
"paragraph,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/6
msgid ""
"land, sea, and air forces, as well as other war\n"
"potential, will never be maintained.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/7
msgid ""
"The right of belligerency of the state will not be\n"
"recognized.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/8
msgid ""
"You know it by heart?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/9
msgid ""
"Some things you never forget.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/10
msgid ""
"Impressive. There were some parts I didn't quite\n"
"get, though\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/11
msgid ""
"- like the whole \"means of settling conflicts\" thing.\n"
msgstr ""
